      "text": "To find the distance between two points in a coordinate plane, we can use the distance formula, which is derived from the Pythagorean theorem. The distance formula is given by:\n\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} \\]\n\nGiven the points \\((-3, -4)\\) and \\((4, -5)\\), we can assign:\n- \\(x_1 = -3\\)\n- \\(y_1 = -4\\)\n- \\(x_2 = 4\\)\n- \\(y_2 = -5\\)\n\nSubstituting these values into the distance formula, we get:\n\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(4 + 3)^2 + (-5 + 4)^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{7^2 + (-1)^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{49 + 1} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{50} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{25 \\times 2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{25} \\times \\sqrt{2} \\]\n\\[ d = 5\\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nThus, the distance between the points \\((-3, -4)\\) and \\((4, -5)\\) is \\(5\\sqrt{2}\\).\n\n**Final answer:** \n\\[ \\boxed{5\\sqrt{2}} \\]",
